AB  - In today's data-driven world, organizations are producing, processing, and analyzing vast volumes of data at unprecedented speeds. To keep up with this rapid pace without compromising accuracy, collaboration among team members, and efficiency in operating the software product, a new variant of DevOps, also known as DataOps, has emerged. Much like DevOps, which brought cultural transformation to software development, DataOps applies agile principles and automation to the data life cycle—streamlining everything from data ingestion and validation to deployment and monitoring of data pipelines. This chapter introduces the data-intensive application and core concepts of DataOps, explains its life cycle, compares it with related practices like DevOps, MLOps, and AIOps, and explores key tools and real-world applications.
