AB  - Software development uses a variety of techniques, such as Agile, Waterfall, and Development and Operations (DevOps), which offer various ways to manage projects. The area of Information Technology (IT) is changing with the emergence of technologies like mobile development, cloud computing, and artificial intelligence. The inaccurate estimation of software development projects leads to huge losses in financial resources available for the project, as well as time required to complete it. To tackle these issues, a LeNet-fused Shepard Convolutional Neural Network (LeNet-ShCNN) approach is developed for software development effort (SDE) prediction. Initially, input software data is obtained from a specific dataset to perform SDE prediction. Then, suitable features are selected in feature selection by Chi-square similarity and Angular separation distance. Finally, SDE prediction is conducted by implementing a newly designed LeNet-ShCNN. The LeNet-ShCNN is the combination of two networks, namely LeNet and the Shepard Convolutional Neural Network (ShCNN). In addition, LeNet-ShCNN acquired a minimum Mean Magnitude Relative Error (MMRE) of 0.147, a minimum Mean Square Error (MSE) of 0.137, and a minimum Root Mean Square Error (RMSE) of 0.370.
